{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1122189-alternate-strider-curse","id":1122189,"title":"Alternate Strider Curse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-28T20:38:52-07:00","id":1122189,"title":"Alternate Strider Curse","content":"Hey everyone.<br /> <br /> I just thought of an alternative to the Silent Strider being chased from Egypt. Basically Seth's Curse align Silent Strider held Caern to open in the Shadowlands rather than the Umbra. Silent Striders Totem are spirits of death and strange ghost-spirits hybrids (NWOD Geists) while their ancestors spirits become wraiths.<br /> <br /> Thoughts on that? Is this too punitive?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T20:53:03-07:00","id":1122199,"title":"","content":"How is that a curse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T21:11:59-07:00","id":1122204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1122189-alternate-strider-curse?p=1122199#post1122199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is that a curse?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are tainted with death-essence, are cut from the very spirit hierarchy you are meant to serve, are apparenttly different from your brothers in arms on the spiritual level. Your ancestors have to deal with Maelstroms and develop Shadows like any other wraiths meaning they're vastly unreliable. Any place you claim as your own is swarmed in ghosts attracted by the openings in the Shroud.<br /> <br /> And that's not even dealing with how the Garou Nation would take such a state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T22:02:09-07:00","id":1122219,"title":"","content":"Sounds like too much crossover work to me imo. Being divorced from the spirit hierarchy means they stop being Garou and are some wonky death wolf thing that's not even in line with the spirit of the game. It sounds to me its like you want a Wraith version of an abomination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 07-29-2017, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T00:07:24-07:00","id":1122250,"title":"","content":"Well mostly because caerns just don't work like that. Caerns are not actually tied to tribe at all. Garou can - and often have - taken caerns from each other. Or sometimes a sept dies off and the caern has to be rediscovered. Is a caern created by a Strider master of the rite a &quot;strider caern&quot; even if most of the Garou there are Fianna? What if the totem isn't of Owl's brood? <br /> <br /> And this is without the question of how a vampire - even a really powerful one - would be able ot so completely alter the very function of the umbra in this way. His curse on the tribe as-written is already in the realm of hand-wavey &quot;Plotdevicum Discipline&quot; territory, and has the logic of sympathetic connection due to the vampires having killed a lot of those ancestors they were taking away from the Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T06:10:28-07:00","id":1122310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1122189-alternate-strider-curse?p=1122250#post1122250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> His curse on the tribe as-written is already in the realm of hand-wavey &quot;Plotdevicum Discipline&quot; territory (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you consider the curse Set put on the Silent Striders Tribe to be so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-29-2017, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T07:44:56-07:00","id":1122335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1122189-alternate-strider-curse?p=1122310#post1122310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you consider the curse Set put on the Silent Striders Tribe to be so?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The strider's curse is too vast. The complexity of what the curse does to them is beyond anything described in any of the systems and it spans many generations beyond when the curse was cast. There is no example of such power being demonstrated in any of the existing material. It would require something of the mythical 10th level to accomplish what Set did, the kind of power only the 3rd generation and lower can muster in game terms. Its the kind of Darkness that not even the tribes Totem can aid in rectifying otherwise it would have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T12:20:50-07:00","id":1122421,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that the Set's Curse did two things.<br /> <br /> 1) Cut off Silent Strider's from their Ancestors (characters cannot obtain the Ancestors background).<br /> <br /> 2) Exile them from the land of Khem (which I assume to mean the Nile Valley from the Delta to the first cataract plus the closest oases, what would be considered to be the boundaries of Egypt at the time of the Curse).since if they stayed there they'd be plagued by terrible nightmares that would prevent them from regaining Gnosis.<br /> <br /> The canonical curse seems fine to me. It has very easy effects for an ST to adjudicate and PCs to understand. It makes sense why Set would curse them as such (which the OP's curse does not). It is devastating to the tribe in character, yet PCs of the tribe are perfectly playable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T12:43:51-07:00","id":1122431,"title":"","content":"The basis for my curse (which I get now is a bad idea) is the Silent Strider marked-in-fluff tendency to be ghosts magnets. This is massively overshadowed by their role as the nomadic tribe but that's a big part of their tribebooks and indeed what the comics to the 2e Tribebook is all about; That was a lame way to emphasize the Necromancer archetype of the tribe rather than the Wanderer. It was also influenced by the White Howlers tribebook which placed the WH as filling a bit of the same niche. .<br /> <br /> The curse would have work through the fact that Silent Striders are already serving a spirit of death.Depending on how you interpret ghostly essence (don't remember if there's a rule somewhere) it could result in the whole tribe smelling faintly of the Wyrm just like the Euthanato\u00ef; That and their links to the realm of the dead would have made the Silent Striders one of the esoteric tribe (which they are admitedly already) with an unique point of view on the Wyrm since they can interact with what happens if things are not destroyed in time.<br /> <br /> As for cross-over, well the Striders are the Wraith tribe just as the Fianna are the Changeling tribe and if I remember the Uktena have some plot hooks involving Dreamspeakers. Hell their Tribe Falls segment has them doing crossover with Orpheus. Unlike actually Vampire, Wraith is topical to Apocalypse as it puts the werewolves in front of memories of their victims and the consequences of their rage and their war. I mean the number of Wraiths killed by werewolves must be pretty close to the number of those killed by vampires.<br /> <br /> Well I continue to think that &quot;The reason Silent Striders have no ancestors is that they are busy keeping Seth in Duat&quot; is still useable, as well as Garous making something with Haunts and openings in the Shroud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T18:36:22-07:00","id":1122559,"title":"","content":"The tribal weakness was always optional. If you are looking for ways to increase crossover with Wraith, or just build on the &quot;ghost magnets&quot; fluff, I think Rites, Gifts, and Merits/Flaws would work best. There are lots of things you can do to built on that based either on Owl as a totem of death, or through Set's Curse. One thing I like to do with my NPCs is have particular merits/flaws show up in a specific ancestral line of Garou. So perhaps the descendants of a particular Silent Strider who fought Set might have been individually cursed so that if they botch certain rites or umbral rolls, they miss the normal Penumbra and interact more with the Dark Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T20:01:28-07:00","id":1125061,"title":"","content":"Just remember: Cursed with Awesomeness is Not A Curse.<br /> <br /> Curses, flaws, derangments are things that must cause you troubles, not give you cool abilities. That's why they give you extra points at character creation.<br /> Giving striders easy access to the dark umbra means giving the Garou a lot of power on a side of the Umbra on which they currently have none. Even assuming you could mystically tie a Tribe to each Caern it would not actually be a disadvantage, since it would not hamper any Strider's activity.<br /> <br /> My old storyteller, time ago, made us meet a Silent Strider that was cursed to only step sideways in the shadowlands... but having this thing on every Strider means that your party automatically splits every time they have to enter the Umbra. It's just not playable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}